## Top Risks

Six risks are tracked in the project risk register, and none is rated above medium-high. The four highest-scoring risks are below.

| Risk | Business Impact | Response | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Legacy POS limitations.** Older point-of-sale systems may not support inventory updates in under 5 seconds. | Inventory accuracy target at risk; possible stockouts or overselling | Early testing of POS connections and custom connectors | Solution Architect |
| **Store network reliability.** Weak Wi-Fi in some of the 45 stores could prevent handheld devices from syncing. | Associates unable to pick or audit orders in some stores | Offline mode on devices; network audit before each store rollout | Solution Architect |
| **Associate training completion.** Staff may not finish onboarding within the 2-hour target. | Disruption to store operations; slower adoption | Short modular training; pilot at high-volume stores first | Business Analyst |
| **Integration cost overrun.** Unexpected complexity could push software costs past the $650K allocation. | Erodes the projected $31K savings | Close spending oversight; approval required for any added features | Project Manager |

